  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nHigh pressure remains centered across Quebec through today,  \ngradually shifting south of New England through the weekend. A \npressure gradient between exiting low pressure in the open\nAtlantic and incoming high pressure will bring one more day of \nbreezy conditions.\n\nAs the high crests overhead tonight, the dry airmass allows for\na cold night with lows falling into the 20s for most of the \narea, and some teens across the north. The high continues to \nmove southward, setting up a moderating southwest flow by the \nend of the weekend. Temps rebound back into the 60s for Sunday \nand Monday.\n\nA weak front passes through on Monday with little more than a \nfew sprinkles across the north. Behind the front, a new high \npressure center arrives with a cooler airmass. Highs return to \nthe 40s and 50s for Tuesday and Wednesday, before beginning to \nrebound back into the 60s for the end of the week as the high \nmoves offshore.\n\nAt this time there is still no meaningful rainfall in the \nforecast for at least the next week.",
